---
title: Generic Curry Base
note: Works for any curry -- prawn, chicken tikka, paneer, etc.
---
Chop @onion{1/2%cup} and @tomatoes{1/2%cup} in roughly equal amounts.

Heat a pan over medium and add enough @sunflower oil{}.

Add @jeera{} and let it sizzle.

Add the onion and a @salt{pinch}. Cook and stir until softened.

Stir in @ginger garlic paste{1%tsp}.

Add the tomatoes and sear.

Reduce heat to low, cover with a lid, and let it cook. Stir occasionally from the sides toward the middle. until softened

Add a pinch each of @haldi{}, @laal mirchi{}, and @dhaniya powder{}. Add @salt{} to taste.

Add @water{1%cup} a little at a time to reach your desired consistency.

Add your protein or main -- prawns, chicken tikka, paneer, etc. -- and toss around for a bit.

Serve.
